ModelUsage.description:
What the model provider reported for the call that produced an agent's turn (15.3, rule 10): the
SDK reads it from the response of every call `wrap()` sees, or takes it from the caller. Optional;
only the agent's own turns carry it.

post.description:
The constraints block of one subject, the one `include: ["constraints"]` adds to a context read;
`for` asks for a beneficiary's. With `tool`, it comes rendered through the tool's binding for this
source, in advisory mode; 422 when the space binds no such tool for it.
